-Obesity increases operative difficulty (deeper scrotum, harder reservoir access). In the 26-case fungal infection series cited by the review, 18/26 (69%) had diabetes and 22/26 (85%) were overweight or obese; these case-only proportions do not estimate risk among all implant recipients.<sup>[[8]](#ref8)[[46]](#ref46)</sup> BMI &gt;30 warrants additional counseling on technical difficulty and infection risk. A retrospective claims cohort of 18,475 IPP recipients reported three-year coded infection in 5.2% of those with recorded obesity versus 3.0% with no identified risk factors (univariate HR 1.76, 95% CI 1.28–2.43).<sup>[[47]](#ref47)</sup> In a revision candidate with BMI &gt;40, weight reduction before reimplantation is a reasonable consideration.
